── (#518) HOLDERS: do Berkshire's and the superinvestors' adds pick winners? (12y forward, stocks) ──
  excess = forward return minus the same-cutoff stock peer mean; hit = excess > 0. Each cohort is
  read against the stock samples outside it. A sample is flagged by the moves FILED in the 135 days
  before its cutoff, each manager's newest one counting: no look-ahead. 0 tickers carry moves.
  CAVEATS: (#737) 13F before 2013-Q2 is read from its text table, kept only when its rows add up to
  the cover's value total (none printed: no row-shaped line left unread), else the quarter folds into
  the next; the 83 managers were picked in 2026, so survivor bias flatters their rows; cutoffs overlap,
